    {
      "id": "IK-869439:L168",
      "source_document": "869439",
      "original_line": 168,
      "text": "> 3. If there was such sub-letting, it had been made with the written consent of the landlord so was not actionable.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "869439",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/869439/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/legal-rule-support-study-02/sources/raw/869439-window0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "252fd6e4ea1f0fd00be5c0d81d43cb82d6c2a0bbdd91d99aaf1c1c21cf7ee9ac",
          "raw_char_range": [
            8450,
            8566
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            8616,
            8732
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 164,
          "original_line": 168
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-869439:L169",
      "source_document": "869439",
      "original_line": 169,
      "text": "The Rent Control Tribunal confirmed the findings against the appellant in all the three contentions and the High Court also affirmed the findings of the Rent Control Tribunal. We must note that no contention was raised before us as far as point No. 1, namely notice was not served. The only contention before us was that there was no sub-letting or parting of the possession by the appellant-tenant in favour of R.C. Abrol & Company Pvt. Ltd.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "869439",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/869439/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/legal-rule-support-study-02/sources/raw/869439-window0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "252fd6e4ea1f0fd00be5c0d81d43cb82d6c2a0bbdd91d99aaf1c1c21cf7ee9ac",
          "raw_char_range": [
            8573,
            9015
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            8739,
            9181
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 165,
          "original_line": 169
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-869439:L170",
      "source_document": "869439",
      "original_line": 170,
      "text": "and secondly it was urged that if there was sub-letting that had been made with the written consent of the landlord. The Clause 14 of the lease deed in the instant case which provides, inter alia, the terms and conditions is as follows:-",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "869439",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/869439/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/legal-rule-support-study-02/sources/raw/869439-window0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "252fd6e4ea1f0fd00be5c0d81d43cb82d6c2a0bbdd91d99aaf1c1c21cf7ee9ac",
          "raw_char_range": [
            9022,
            9259
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            9188,
            9425
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 166,
          "original_line": 170
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-869439:L171",
      "source_document": "869439",
      "original_line": 171,
      "text": "> \"Clause 14-That the lessee undertakes not to sub- let the premises to any other party without the written permission of the lessor, and that the lessee's contractors M/s R.C. Abrol & Co. will share the premises with the permission of the lessor.\"",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "869439",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/869439/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/legal-rule-support-study-02/sources/raw/869439-window0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "252fd6e4ea1f0fd00be5c0d81d43cb82d6c2a0bbdd91d99aaf1c1c21cf7ee9ac",
          "raw_char_range": [
            9266,
            9514
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            9432,
            9680
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 167,
          "original_line": 171
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-869439:L176",
      "source_document": "869439",
      "original_line": 176,
      "text": "Before us it was pointed out by Sree Shankar Ghosh, learned counsel for the appellant, that it was not necessary that the consent to sub-letting should be in writing and what he contended was that it was necessary to have the consent and the manner of proving consent was provided in writing.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "869439",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/869439/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/legal-rule-support-study-02/sources/raw/869439-window0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "252fd6e4ea1f0fd00be5c0d81d43cb82d6c2a0bbdd91d99aaf1c1c21cf7ee9ac",
          "raw_char_range": [
            10155,
            10447
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            10337,
            10629
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 172,
          "original_line": 176
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-869439:L177@0:232",
      "source_document": "869439",
      "original_line": 177,
      "text": "In other words, he contended that the provision which required that the consent should be in writing meant it was mandatory so far as it enjoined consent but it was directory so far as it said that such consent should be in writing.",
      "provenance": [
        {
          "document_id": "869439",
          "url": "https://indiankanoon.org/doc/869439/",
          "response_index": 0,
          "raw_path": "outputs/legal-rule-support-study-02/sources/raw/869439-window0.txt",
          "raw_sha256": "252fd6e4ea1f0fd00be5c0d81d43cb82d6c2a0bbdd91d99aaf1c1c21cf7ee9ac",
          "raw_char_range": [
            10454,
            10942
          ],
          "raw_byte_range": [
            10636,
            11132
          ],
          "raw_physical_line": 173,
          "original_line": 177
        }
      ],
      "source_segment_id": "IK-869439:L177",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 232
    },
    {
      "id": "IK-869439:L225",
      "source_document": "869439",
      "original_line": 225,
      "text": "Dr. Shankar Ghosh drew our attention to the observations of the High Court of Delhi in the following three cases:",
